{
  "title": "Practice: index laws",
  "intro": "Eleven questions on the index laws. Where a box asks for a power, type just the number — for example -3.",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "i3-q1",
      "type": "flashcards",
      "prompt": "Flip through the index laws. Say each one out loud before you turn the card over.",
      "cards": [
        { "id": "c1", "front": "$a^x \\times a^y$", "back": "$a^{x+y}$ — same base, **add** the powers" },
        { "id": "c2", "front": "$a^x \\div a^y$", "back": "$a^{x-y}$ — same base, **subtract** the powers" },
        { "id": "c3", "front": "$(a^x)^y$", "back": "$a^{xy}$ — power of a power, **multiply**" },
        { "id": "c4", "front": "$a^0$", "back": "$1$, for any non-zero $a$" },
        { "id": "c5", "front": "$a^{-n}$", "back": "$\\frac{1}{a^n}$ — the reciprocal of $a^n$" },
        { "id": "c6", "front": "$10^{-3}$", "back": "$\\frac{1}{1000} = 0.001$" },
        { "id": "c7", "front": "BIDMAS", "back": "Brackets, Indices, Division/Multiplication, Addition/Subtraction" }
      ],
      "explanation": "These seven facts cover every question in this lesson. The one people forget is that a negative index means **one over**, not a negative number."
    },
    {
      "id": "i3-q2",
      "type": "numeric",
      "prompt": "Write $3^{-2}$ as a fraction.",
      "answer": "1/9",
      "accept": ["0.111", "0.1111"],
      "tolerance": 0.001,
      "hints": ["$a^{-n} = \\frac{1}{a^n}$", "What is $3^2$?"],
      "explanation": "$3^{-2} = \\frac{1}{3^2} = \\frac{1}{9}$.",
      "difficulty": "foundation"
    },
    {
      "id": "i3-q3",
      "type": "fill-blank",
      "prompt": "Write each number as a power of 2 by filling in the missing index.",
      "text": "$8 = 2^{\\square}$ : [[a]] $\\qquad 2 = 2^{\\square}$ : [[b]] $\\qquad \\frac{1}{2} = 2^{\\square}$ : [[c]] $\\qquad \\frac{1}{16} = 2^{\\square}$ : [[d]] $\\qquad 1 = 2^{\\square}$ : [[e]]",
      "blanks": [
        { "id": "a", "accept": ["3"], "size": 3 },
        { "id": "b", "accept": ["1"], "size": 3 },
        { "id": "c", "accept": ["-1", "−1"], "size": 3 },
        { "id": "d", "accept": ["-4", "−4"], "size": 3 },
        { "id": "e", "accept": ["0"], "size": 3 }
      ],
      "hints": ["$16 = 2^4$, so $\\frac{1}{16}$ is the reciprocal of $2^4$."],
      "explanation": "$8 = 2^3$, $2 = 2^1$, $\\frac{1}{2} = 2^{-1}$, $\\frac{1}{16} = \\frac{1}{2^4} = 2^{-4}$, and $1 = 2^0$."
    },
    {
      "id": "i3-q4",
      "type": "match",
      "prompt": "Match each power of 3 to its value.",
