      "explanation": "a: both are 1 ✗. b: $\\frac{1}{8} < \\frac{1}{4}$ ✗. c: $6^{-3} = \\frac{1}{216}$, which is positive ✗. d: $(-2)^{-1} = -\\frac{1}{2}$, which is less than 0.5 ✓. e: $-3^2 = -9$ (the power is done before the minus), which is less than 0 ✓.",
      "difficulty": "challenge"
    },
    {
      "id": "i3-q7",
      "type": "fill-blank",
      "prompt": "Simplify each expression, leaving your answer in index form. Type only the missing power.",
      "text": "$5^{-7} \\times 5^5 = 5^{\\square}$ : [[a]] $\\qquad 2^{-1} \\div 2^5 = 2^{\\square}$ : [[b]] $\\qquad (6^3)^{-2} = 6^{\\square}$ : [[c]] $\\qquad 11^{-8} \\times 11^2 \\times 11^3 = 11^{\\square}$ : [[d]]",
      "blanks": [
        { "id": "a", "accept": ["-2", "−2"], "size": 3 },
        { "id": "b", "accept": ["-6", "−6"], "size": 3 },
        { "id": "c", "accept": ["-6", "−6"], "size": 3 },
        { "id": "d", "accept": ["-3", "−3"], "size": 3 }
      ],
      "hints": [
        "Multiplying: add. Dividing: subtract. Power of a power: multiply.",
        "Be careful with signs: $-1 - 5 = -6$."
      ],
      "explanation": "$-7 + 5 = -2$. $-1 - 5 = -6$. $3 \\times -2 = -6$. $-8 + 2 + 3 = -3$."
    },
    {
      "id": "i3-q8",
      "type": "order",
      "prompt": "Put the steps for simplifying $\\dfrac{(3^6 \\times 3^4)^2}{3^2 \\times 3^3}$ in the correct order.",
      "items": [
        { "id": "s1", "text": "Inside the top bracket: $3^6 \\times 3^4 = 3^{10}$" },
        { "id": "s2", "text": "Apply the power: $(3^{10})^2 = 3^{20}$" },
        { "id": "s3", "text": "Simplify the bottom: $3^2 \\times 3^3 = 3^5$" },
        { "id": "s4", "text": "Divide: $3^{20} \\div 3^5 = 3^{15}$" }
      ],
      "solution": ["s1", "s2", "s3", "s4"],
      "hints": ["Brackets before indices, and the dividing line acts like a bracket."],
      "explanation": "Brackets first, then the power on the bracket, then finish the denominator, and only then divide. Doing the division first would ignore the brackets that the long dividing line creates."
    },
    {
      "id": "i3-q9",
